{
 "label": "/REWIND · CLAUDE CODE",
 "accentWords": [
  "wrong",
  "rewind",
  "git",
  "catch",
  "save",
  "follow",
  "undo",
  "tracks",
  "restore",
  "summarize"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "text": "Claude Code just edited your files in the wrong direction. You don't have to undo it by hand.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "hero",
    "headA": "IT EDITED THE",
    "headB": "WRONG FILES",
    "icon": "rewind",
    "node": {
     "t": "UNDO IT: /rewind",
     "at": "undo",
     "cls": "acc",
     "sym": "«"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "text": "Claude Code tracks every edit it makes with its file tools. Type slash rewind, or press escape twice, to open the menu.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "stack",
    "items": [
     {
      "k": "term",
      "text": "/rewind",
      "at": "slash"
     },
     {
      "k": "chips",
      "label": "or press",
      "chips": [
       {
        "t": "Esc",
        "at": "escape"
       },
       {
        "t": "Esc",
        "at": "twice"
       },
       {
        "t": "on an empty prompt",
        "cls": "am",
        "at": "menu"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "title": "OPEN THE MENU"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "text": "Pick a point in the session, then restore the code, the conversation, or both. Or summarize from there to free up context.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "stack",
    "items": [
     {
      "k": "rows",
      "label": "/rewind menu",
      "rows": [
       {
        "t": "Restore code",
        "at": "code"
       },
       {
        "t": "Restore conversation",
        "at": "conversation"
       },
       {
        "t": "Restore code and conversation",
        "at": "both",
        "cls": "hot"
       },
       {
        "t": "Summarize from here",
        "at": "summarize",
        "cls": "dim"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "title": "PICK WHAT TO RESTORE"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "text": "But there's a catch. If a file was changed only by a shell command, rewind doesn't track it. Edits made by subagents usually aren't captured either.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "stack",
    "items": [
     {
      "k": "warn",
      "label": "rewind does not undo",
      "items": [
       {
        "t": "Bash-only file changes",
        "at": "shell"
       },
       {
        "t": "subagent edits (usually)",
        "at": "subagents"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "title": "THE CATCH"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "text": "So rewind is not a replacement for git. For those changes, git is what brings them back.",
   "stamp": {
    "text": [
     "REWIND",
     "≠ GIT"
    ],
    "at": "git"
   },
   "scene": {
    "type": "stack",
    "items": [
     {
      "k": "rows",
      "label": "who undoes what",
      "rows": [
       {
        "t": "/rewind",
        "tag": "Claude's tracked edits",
        "at": "rewind"
       },
       {
        "t": "git",
        "tag": "everything else",
        "cls": "hot",
        "at": "git"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "s6",
   "text": "Save this for your next session. Follow for more Claude Code workflows.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "cta"
   }
  }
 ]
}